"@@note:ก็ gôr is one of the most common words in Thai. Its meaning depends heavily on context, so it often cannot be translated with a single English word.\n\nIts most common use is \"also\" or \"too\".\n\nผมก็ชอบ pŏm gôr chôp = I like it too. / I also like it.\n\nIn many sentences, ก็ gôr can also connect ideas, add emphasis, or simply help a sentence flow more naturally without contributing a clear meaning of its own. It is therefore often best understood from the whole sentence rather than translated literally."
